// A scalar constant whose initialiser is a bare `(import other)` is emitted
// as the initialiser of the constant it names, because a file-scope
// initialiser must be a constant expression and a read of another global is
// not one. The parser does this for an earlier constant (front/parse/decl/top/
// marker/const/fold.id), but a later constant, or one from a conf.id that
// sorts after this one, is not known yet when the import is parsed, so the
// backends finish the job here, on the finished tables, where order no longer
// matters. The node tables are left alone: the case cache reads a constant's
// edges from the import node, which stays where it was parsed.
//
// const_root follows the chain one hop per constant at most, so a cycle ends
// at an import node, which both C and LLVM then reject as a read of a global.

const_root(int e) {
  int hops = 0;
  while(hops < len((import cdecl))) {
    e = const_hop(e);
    hops = hops + 1;
  }
} return int e;
